<v Valdo>This sound happens in stressed "i" and word final "e".

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:43.650
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>E</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>vê</lang>, <lang pt-BR>vejo</lang>, <lang pt-BR>você</lang>, <lang pt-BR>levamos</lang>.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.450
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>É</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>pé</lang>, <lang pt-BR>pedra</lang>, <lang pt-BR>até</lang>.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.500
<v Valdo>This sound happens in stressed syllables only.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.000
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>A</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>pá</lang>,

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.780
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>pato</lang>, <lang pt-BR>dará</lang>, <lang pt-BR>falamos</lang>.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:08.500
<v Valdo>We have <lang pt-BR>ó</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>pó</lang>, <lang pt-BR>pode</lang>, <lang pt-BR>avó</lang>.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:13.250
<v Valdo>This also only happens in stressed syllables.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.530
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>Ô</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>pôde</lang>, <lang pt-BR>avô</lang>, <lang pt-BR>podemos</lang>.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:30.250
<v Valdo><lang pt-BR>U</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>pude</lang>, <lang pt-BR>urubu</lang>, <lang pt-BR>vivo</lang>: stressed "u" and word final "o".

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:36.000
<v Michelle><lang pt-BR>A</lang> as in <lang pt-BR>viva</lang>, <lang pt-BR>coma</lang>.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.000
<v Orlando>There are also nasal vowel sounds in Portuguese.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.750
<v Orlando>And so let's get a chance to hear
